{{- template "require-profile" . -}}
{{- $caps := index .profiles .profile "capabilities" -}}
{{- /* GitHub injection guard (epic #119). Best-effort / steering only:
       command-string matchers are bypassable ($(), equivalent read paths like
       xxd / python open(), MCP by other means) and are NOT an enforcement
       boundary — see docs/ai-environment-boundary.md and the bypass
       negative test in scripts/test-claude-settings.sh. deny = never-OK (hard);
       ask = always needs approval.

       Three deny tiers (#119 Phase 2 task B):
       1. never-legit secret floor (UNCONDITIONAL): reading SSH private keys or
          credential-store files (gh OAuth token, AWS keys, ~/.netrc, Codex
          auth.json, OpenCode auth.json — #234), dumping the whole env,
          touching GitHub Actions secrets, printing the gh token (`gh auth
          token`, `gh auth status --show-token|-t`, incl. the `-at` bundle;
          `gh auth` with options before `auth` or right after it is denied
          as a whole, since those placements reach the same subcommands) or
          reading / dumping / exporting keychain passwords with `security`
          (with or without leading options such as `-q`) (#315, symmetric
          with the OpenCode floor and the Codex probes)
          is never something the human legitimately asks Claude (the AI tool) to
          do, and a deny binds only Claude's own Bash tool calls — never the
          human's own terminal, and not env calls nested inside a script Claude
          runs. So this floor is always on at ~zero human friction, making the
          secret floor (epic #119) live on personal WITHOUT enforceAiSandbox's
          egress block. Read() denies are the PRIMARY axis (they bind the Read
          tool regardless of which command would print the file); the Bash
          matchers are bypassable steering (head/xxd/python open() slip through),
          so per-path Bash enumeration is deliberately NOT attempted (#136).
       2. gateGitHubMcp: deny the github MCP server.
       The unconditional ask is the whole 1Password CLI (`op *`, #315): its
       secret-producing subcommands (read / item get / run / inject / document
       get / signin --raw ...) take global options anywhere, so the program,
       not a subcommand list, is the unit. The human does direct those (e.g.
       private-backup --identity-command), so approval, not deny.
       Destructive git, hook skips and the reference note (#304, after
       agent-tools#204 left them to the hosts' permissions; unconditional,
       steering like the rest):
       - ask: work-discarding git — reset --hard, clean, checkout -- <path> /
         checkout <...> . / checkout or switch with -f / --force /
         --discard-changes, restore, push with --force / -f / a +refspec
         (--force-with-lease is not matched), branch -D / --force / -f. The
         human does direct these, so approval. An option counts only as a
         word of its own (`git *push* -f`, `git *push* -f *`), wherever it sits
         after its subcommand, and global options may precede the
         subcommand (`git -C dir`); so a branch named feature-f is not a
         force (Codex review R1, PR #326). Representative two-letter short
         bundles are listed too (push -uf / -fu, branch -df / -fd, checkout
         and switch -qf / -fq); other bundles and abbreviated long options
         are not — spelling variants are not enumerated (the #315 lesson).
         The price is an occasional extra prompt (a commit message naming
         such a command), harmless for ask. Words that appear in prose
         (clean, restore) keep a space on each side. The (subcommand, option)
         pairs below generate both rules of each pair.
       - deny: hook skips — --no-verify on any git command and `git commit -n`
         (its short form). Skipping the pre-commit / commit-msg gates
         (git-hook-gates) is never something to do from an AI tool; a human
         who needs it runs it in their own terminal. A glob cannot tell an
         option from quoted data (`git commit -m "document --no-verify"`), so
         deny is kept to the places data cannot take — the last word of the
         command, or right after `git commit` / `git push` — and every other
         placement (global options, mid-command, bundles -nm / -an / -anm, a
         quoted mention) is ask (Codex review R1, PR #326). Not covered:
         other bundles, abbreviated long options, `-c core.hooksPath=...`.
       - deny: Edit on any .agent-context.local.md — the agent reads that
         user-owned note and never writes it. An Edit deny also binds Write,
         NotebookEdit and Bash file commands / redirections that name the
         path, not scripts that open it themselves.
       3. enforceAiSandbox (human-legit, stays gated): git push to main/master and
          reading .env are things the human does legitimately direct Claude to do,
          so they ride on enforceAiSandbox — which personal keeps false because its
          egress block is unusable on a daily driver. The restricted-context
          launcher meant to carry these (a session started with claude
          --settings stacked on this template) is not built (#131 closed
          without it; no tracking issue). The context-gated writes (merge/PR/
          comment/label/push ai/*) would need a context-gated write hook, which
          is not built either (#131 closed without it; no tracking issue; the
          #137 hook below only steers reads), so they are intentionally absent.

       enableGitHubIsolatedReader (#137) registers the PreToolUse read-steering
       hook (matcher Bash): agent-tools deploys the body (personal-safe-gh-hook)
       to a stable path (agent-tools#146 contract) and dotfiles only references
       it by absolute path — no script body is distributed from here. The hook
       nudges raw `gh` reads of untrusted GitHub content toward the safe-gh
       isolated reader. Steering / fail-open: a missing body (exit 127), any
       non-2 non-zero exit, bad JSON, or a timeout all let the tool call
       continue (only exit 2 blocks), so registering before agent-tools has
       synced is a safe no-op. This is NOT the context-gated write hook above.

       enableQualityLoopHooks (#199, agent-tools#203) registers the two
       quality-loop lifecycle hooks the same way (registration here, bodies
       agent-tools-deployed): PostToolUse / Edit|Write -> personal-fast-edit-
       check (steering, never blocks) and Stop -> personal-changed-scope-qa
       (best-effort gate: blocks once per new dirty scope, never when
       stop_hook_active). Both are silent no-ops until a repo is declared in
       the user-owned ~/.config/agent-tools/checks.local.json.

       enableHerdrIntegration (#225, agent-tools#252 hand-off) registers
       herdr's SessionStart hook (matcher "^(startup|resume|clear|compact|fork)$", herdr
       0.9.3 / #274) the same way, with the body
       owned by herdr instead of agent-tools: `herdr integration install
       claude` writes ~/.claude/hooks/herdr-agent-state.sh, and the entry is
       rendered in exactly the shape that installer emits, so it recognizes
       the managed registration and leaves settings.json untouched (measured
       byte-identical). Session-id report only, from inside a herdr pane;
       exits 0 elsewhere.

       The whole "hooks" object is shared with the Codex registration via
       .chezmoitemplates/agent-hooks-json (#181 parity — edit it once there);
       it is included only when at least one hook capability is on, so an
       empty "hooks": {} is never emitted. */ -}}
{{- $deny := list "Read(~/.ssh/**)" "Read(~/.aws/**)" "Read(~/.config/gh/**)" "Read(~/.netrc)" "Read(~/.codex/auth.json)" "Read(~/.local/share/opencode/auth.json)" "Bash(cat ~/.ssh/*)" "Bash(gh secret *)" "Bash(gh api *secrets*)" "Bash(env)" "Bash(env *)" "Bash(printenv)" "Bash(printenv *)" "Bash(gh auth token)" "Bash(gh auth token *)" "Bash(gh auth status *--show-token*)" "Bash(gh auth status -t*)" "Bash(gh auth status * -t*)" "Bash(gh auth status -at*)" "Bash(gh auth status * -at*)" "Bash(gh -* auth *)" "Bash(gh auth -*)" "Bash(security find-generic-password *)" "Bash(security * find-generic-password *)" "Bash(security find-internet-password *)" "Bash(security * find-internet-password *)" "Bash(security dump-keychain*)" "Bash(security * dump-keychain*)" "Bash(security export *)" "Bash(security * export *)" "Bash(git * --no-verify)" "Bash(git commit --no-verify *)" "Bash(git push --no-verify *)" "Bash(git commit -n *)" "Bash(git commit * -n)" "Edit(//**/.agent-context.local.md)" -}}
{{- if index $caps "gateGitHubMcp" -}}{{- $deny = concat $deny (list "mcp__github") -}}{{- end -}}
{{- $ask := list "Bash(op *)" "Bash(git clean *)" "Bash(git * clean *)" "Bash(git restore *)" "Bash(git * restore *)" "Bash(git *checkout* -- *)" "Bash(git *checkout* .)" "Bash(git *push* +*)" -}}
{{- range list (list "reset" "--hard") (list "checkout" "--force") (list "checkout" "-f") (list "checkout" "-qf") (list "checkout" "-fq") (list "switch" "--force") (list "switch" "--discard-changes") (list "switch" "-f") (list "switch" "-qf") (list "switch" "-fq") (list "push" "--force") (list "push" "-f") (list "push" "-uf") (list "push" "-fu") (list "branch" "-D") (list "branch" "--force") (list "branch" "-f") (list "branch" "-df") (list "branch" "-fd") (list "commit" "-n") (list "commit" "-nm") (list "commit" "-an") (list "commit" "-anm") -}}
{{- $ask = concat $ask (list (printf "Bash(git *%s* %s)" (index . 0) (index . 1)) (printf "Bash(git *%s* %s *)" (index . 0) (index . 1))) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $ask = append $ask "Bash(git *--no-verify*)" -}}
{{- if index $caps "enforceAiSandbox" -}}{{- $deny = concat $deny (list "Bash(cat *.env*)" "Read(//**/.env*)" "Bash(git push * main)" "Bash(git push * master)") -}}{{- $ask = concat $ask (list "Bash(gh release create *)" "Bash(gh release delete *)" "Bash(gh release edit *)" "Bash(gh api *protection*)" "Bash(gh api *rulesets*)") -}}{{- end -}}
{
{{- if index $caps "enforceAiSandbox" }}
  "sandbox": {
    "enabled": true,
    "failIfUnavailable": true,
    "allowUnsandboxedCommands": false,
    "network": {
      "allowedDomains": []
    }
  },
{{- end }}
  "permissions": {
{{- if $deny }}
    "deny": {{ $deny | toJson }},
{{- end }}
{{- if $ask }}
    "ask": {{ $ask | toJson }},
{{- end }}
    "allow": [
      "mcp__pencil"
    ]
  },
{{- if or (index $caps "enableGitHubIsolatedReader") (index $caps "enableQualityLoopHooks") (index $caps "enableHerdrIntegration") }}
{{ template "agent-hooks-json" (dict "caps" $caps "homeDir" .chezmoi.homeDir "agentDir" ".claude") }},
{{- end }}
  "model": "opus[1m]",
  "statusLine": {
    "type": "command",
    "command": "{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/go/bin/tacho statusline",
    "padding": 0
  },
  "enabledPlugins": {
    "skill-creator@claude-plugins-official": true,
    "codex@openai-codex": true,
    "notion@claude-plugins-official": true
  },
  "extraKnownMarketplaces": {
    "openai-codex": {
      "source": {
        "source": "github",
        "repo": "openai/codex-plugin-cc",
        "ref": "v1.0.4"
      },
      "autoUpdate": false
    }
  },
  "effortLevel": "xhigh",
  "agentPushNotifEnabled": true,
  "remoteControlAtStartup": true,
  "skipWorkflowUsageWarning": true,
  "tui": "fullscreen"
}
